// Standalone OpenCode provider snippet for the qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3
// service (feat-4 Phase 7), Dell 7960T (hostname sys0).
//
// *** GPU1-OUTAGE STANDBY -- NOT the default production endpoint. ***
// This is a temporary, single-GPU (TP=1, GPU3 only) fallback that exists
// solely because GPU1 has been exhibiting a recurring under-sustained-
// load PCIe-drop fault (see hardware/dell-7960t/recovery.md's incident
// log). For normal use, prefer the production BF16/896K/TP=2 service
// (GPU0+GPU2) documented in this feature folder's own
// opencode-provider-snippet-qwen3.8-27b.jsonc -- use *this* snippet only
// while that GPU pairing is unavailable/degraded, or when explicitly
// asked to validate the standby itself.
//
// Precision/decode note: this endpoint runs NVFP4 + MTP speculative
// decoding. Task 7.4 found MTP output on this GPU3/NVFP4/TP=1 config is
// NOT strictly byte-identical to a non-MTP run on longer/higher-entropy
// generations (root-caused to floating-point non-associativity between
// MTP's batched-verification and single-token decode GEMM shapes, not a
// correctness bug -- every response remained coherent and factually
// correct). Kept enabled per the 2026-09-21 "continue with MTP" decision
// (see Decisions Made) -- flagging here so any consumer of this endpoint
// is aware the exact wording of long free-text completions may differ
// slightly from what a non-speculative run of the same prompt would
// produce.
//
// NOT written into any opencode.jsonc on this box -- paste this into the
// "provider" object of your own opencode.jsonc. Mirrors feat-2/feat-3's
// "standalone snippet" precedent for this repo.
//
// Prerequisites before this endpoint actually answers requests:
//   1. On the Dell 7960T: `qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3 start`
//      (on-demand only -- never auto-started, per REQ-008; the control
//      script refuses to start while qwen3.8-27b-bf16-896k-mtp-2.service
//      is active, since both share GPU3 -- stop that one first if so;
//      stop this one with `qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3 stop` when done,
//      or via `systemctl --user stop qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3.service`)
//   2. Confirm GPU1 is not in use by this standby -- it never is
//      (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES is pinned to GPU3's UUID only), but this is
//      the entire reason this unit exists, so it is worth re-stating
//   3. Replace <sys0-LAN-IP> below with the box's actual current LAN IP
//      (DHCP-assigned, so it can change -- e.g. `192.168.1.103` as of
//      2026-08-25's session; use `localhost`/`127.0.0.1` instead if
//      OpenCode runs on the Dell 7960T itself)
//
// No API key is required or accepted (REQ-007: unauthenticated, internal
// network only, accepted risk) -- if the AI SDK's openai-compatible
// provider errors on a missing key anyway, add "apiKey": "not-needed"
// under "options" (same workaround feat-2/feat-3/the production snippet
// documented).
{
    "qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3-standby": {
        "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
        "name": "Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4+MTP GPU3 standby (Dell 7960T, GPU1-outage fallback)",
        "options": { "baseURL": "http://<sys0-LAN-IP>:8007/v1" },
        "models": {
            "qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3": {
                "name": "qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-mtp-gpu3",
                "limit": { "context": 917504, "output": 65536 }
            }
        }
    }
}
